            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous muscles in the hand and wrist--report of three cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>553-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three cases of anomalous muscles were encountered recently during separate surgical procedures. The first caused a carpal tunnel syndrome by compressing the medium nerve; the second presented as a tumor-like mass in the wrist; and the third was an incidental finding at operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
